\ni In order to see if an element is a power of a second word, we
find their canonical decompositions. These elements must have
the same cyclic factors occurring in their decompositions and there
must be an integer m such that the m-th power of the first word is
the second. If such an integer exists, this can be discerned from
the respective decompositions.

\ni For a general discussion, see
@General_abelian_groups@General_abelian_groups::General discussion@

